What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/identity_override
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		Force the identity of the expansion pack ("sleeve") on the
		iPAQ's single sleeve connector, overriding the vendor:device
		pair read from the pack's ID EEPROM, for packs whose EEPROM
		reads back invalid (all zeros) or cannot be read, so that
		the pack's driver and the slot consumers keyed on identity
		still bind.

		Reading lists "none" followed by every sleeve type the bus
		knows, space-separated; the active override is enclosed in
		square brackets:

		  [none] cf cf_plus pcmcia ... navman_gps_cf ...

		An override naming no listed type is shown after the list
		as a bracketed hexadecimal "VVVV:DDDD" pair.

		Writing a listed name, or a hexadecimal "VVVV:DDDD"
		vendor:device pair, sets the override; writing "none"
		clears it. Either takes effect immediately: a pack on the
		connector is torn down and re-enumerated exactly as on a
		physical re-insertion (power rails cycle, its driver is
		removed and re-probed, slot consumers are notified), now
		carrying the forced identity. With nothing attached the
		override is stored and applied to the next insertion.

		The override describes the connector, not one insertion:
		it persists across removals and insertions until "none" is
		written or the system reboots, and is applied even over a
		readable, valid EEPROM. Each insertion that applies it logs
		a warning naming the forced identity and what the EEPROM
		actually returned. Forcing the wrong type can select the
		wrong slot count or power configuration for the pack.

		Names and the IDs they stand for:
		  cf 1125:cf11, cf_plus 1125:0003, pcmcia 1125:d7c3,
		  pcmcia_plus 1125:0004, dual_pcmcia 1125:0001,
		  bluetooth_cf 1125:0011, gprs 1125:0010,
		  nexian_dual_cf 010a:0001, nexian_camera_cf 010a:0003,
		  symbol_wlan_scanner 0103:0011, pitech_memplug 0111:0001,
		  pitech_memplug3 0111:0003, navman_gps_cf 0100:0001,
		  navman_gps_cf_alt 0100:0010, pcmcia_blank_eeprom ffff:ffff

		The ipaq_sleeve.identity_override= kernel parameter seeds
		the same value at boot and accepts the same strings.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../id_eeprom_valid
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) 1 if the pack's ID EEPROM record was read in full:
		the 0xaa header byte, the description, the fixed fields,
		the 0x0f0f0f0f section marker and the 0xbb byte all
		checked out. 0 otherwise, whether the EEPROM could not be
		read, its header was rejected or a later check failed; the
		kernel log names which.

		This is independent of whether the pack is identified. A
		pack whose header and ID read correctly keeps that
		identity even when a later check fails, and a pack whose
		identity was forced through identity_override reports the
		state of its own EEPROM here, not of the forced type. A
		record read under a forced identity is shown but is not
		acted on.

		The record attributes below exist only while this reads 1.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../vendor
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../device
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) Vendor and device ID the bus matches drivers against,
		as "0x%04x": the pair read from ID EEPROM bytes 6-9, the
		pair forced through identity_override, or 0x0000 for a pack
		that could not be identified.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../type
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) Name of the pack type for vendor and device, from the
		same list identity_override accepts, or "unknown" for a
		pair the bus has no name for or an unidentified pack.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../record_length_raw
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) ID EEPROM bytes 1-4 as a decimal little-endian u32.
		Believed to be the length of the record, which is not
		established; no known consumer reads it. The kernel warns
		when it is shorter than the part of the record that was
		parsed or longer than the 512-byte EEPROM.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../record_version
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../record_format
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) Record layout version from ID EEPROM byte 5, as a
		number (1, 2 or 3) and as "v1", "v2" or "v3". A v1 record
		carries no socket types and no OPT_ON byte.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../description
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) The pack's description string. At most 255
		characters; every byte outside printable ASCII is shown as
		"?".

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../type_raw
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) The record's type byte, as "0x%02x". Its encoding is
		not known and nothing acts on it.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../interrupt_enable_raw
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) The record's interrupt-enable byte, as "0x%02x". Its
		only known use is gating the vendor OS's own sleeve
		interrupt dispatch; it says nothing about whether a pack
		driver needs the OPT_INT line, and nothing acts on it.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../extended_battery
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) 1 if the record's extended-battery byte is 'Y' or
		'y', meaning the pack carries a battery, else 0.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../initial_power_state_raw
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../suspend_power_state_raw
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) The record's initial and suspend power state bytes,
		as "0x%02x". Their encoding is not known and nothing acts
		on them.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../reset_width_ms
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../stabilize_ms
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) Width, in milliseconds, of the OPT_RESET pulse the
		pack asks for after power-up, and the wait after that
		pulse, as decimal numbers. A width of 0 asks for no
		pulse. For a v2 or v3 record with a non-zero width the
		bus pulses OPT_RESET after powering the pack and before
		announcing it to slot drivers, each time clamped to
		1000 ms; v1 records and a forced identity get no pulse.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../unknown_1a_raw
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../unknown_1c_raw
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) The two 16-bit record fields between the stabilisation
		wait and the section marker, as "0x%04x". Every record
		version carries them; their meaning is not known.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../socket0_type
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../socket1_type
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) How the pack connects each PC Card socket: "direct"
		(type 0 or 1, the socket is reset directly),
		"l1110-bridge" (type 2, through a LinkUp L1110 bridge) or
		"unknown (N)" for any other type N. v2 and v3 records
		only.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../opt_on_requested
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) 1 if the record's OPT_ON byte is non-zero, meaning
		the pack asks for its main power rail, else 0. v2 and v3
		records only. The rail is currently switched on for every
		pack regardless.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../memory_window_bytes
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../memory_capable
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) Size of the memory window the record's 0xbb section
		declares, end - start + 1 from its third and fourth words,
		in bytes; 0 if the end lies before the start.
		memory_capable is 1 if that size is at least 1024 bytes,
		the threshold from which the pack is treated as carrying
		memory, else 0.

What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../bb_word1_raw
What:		/sys/bus/ipaq-sleeve/devices/.../bb_word2_raw
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2
Contact:	Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Description:
		(RO) The first two words of the record's 0xbb section, as
		"0x%08x". Their meaning is not known.
